//? Title: UCI Machine Learning Repository datasets
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

> Discover and load UCI tables

The UCI catalog records publisher IDs, names, shapes, exact file sizes, licenses,
creators, DOIs and source URLs. Discovery is offline. The first named load
downloads the original CSV. Later loads use the same local file and verify its
size and SHA-256 before parsing. The CSV payloads stay out of the binary.

```{cpp, id=uci-discovery, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/data.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    const auto sources = dm::datasets::uci_catalog();
    std::println("Registered UCI tables: {}.\n", sources.nrows());
    const auto examples = sources.filter([](const auto& row) {
        const auto name = row.get_string("name");
        return name == "uci_1" || name == "uci_31" || name == "uci_53" || name == "uci_109";
    });
    std::print("{}", examples.select({"name", "alias", "title", "rows", "columns", "bytes", "license", "doi"}).to_md());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Registered UCI tables: 142.

| name | alias | title | rows | columns | bytes | license | doi |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |
| uci_1 | uci_abalone | Abalone | 4177 | 9 | 196140 | CC BY 4.0 | 10.24432/C55C7W |
| uci_31 | uci_covertype | Covertype | 581012 | 55 | 75751077 | CC BY 4.0 | 10.24432/C50K5N |
| uci_53 | uci_iris | Iris | 150 | 5 | 4615 | CC BY 4.0 | 10.24432/C56C76 |
| uci_109 | uci_wine | Wine | 178 | 14 | 11480 | CC BY 4.0 | 10.24432/C5PC7J |
// result_end

> Work with the local cache

`dm::data("uci_abalone")` and `dm::data("uci_1")` select the same source and
cache entry. `dm::data("iris")` continues to return the bundled R-style iris
table. `dm::data("uci_iris")` uses UCI's original CSV schema and class labels.

```{cpp, id=uci-cache, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/data.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    const auto frame = dm::data("uci_iris");
    std::println("The UCI iris snapshot has {} rows and {} columns.", frame.nrows(), frame.ncols());
    std::print("{}", frame.head(3).to_md());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
The UCI iris snapshot has 150 rows and 5 columns.
| sepal length | sepal width | petal length | petal width | class |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |
| 5.1 | 3.5 | 1.4 | 0.2 | Iris-setosa |
| 4.9 | 3.0 | 1.4 | 0.2 | Iris-setosa |
| 4.7 | 3.2 | 1.3 | 0.2 | Iris-setosa |
// result_end

Set `DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR` to choose the cache root. UCI sources live under
`uci_<id>/data.csv`. Set `DATAMUNGE_DATA_OFFLINE=1` to require a local copy,
or use `DATAMUNGE_DATA_MIRROR` for a mirror with the same layout and bytes.
`dm::data()` loads a complete table into memory. To work in batches, pass
the path from `dm::datasets::fetch()` to `dm::datasets::CsvReader`. For
example, use `dm::datasets::fetch("uci_covertype")` for Covertype. The
catalog's `missing` column lists each source's missing-value marker.

> Selection and attribution

The audit starts with UCI's API index. A registered entry has an official,
single, rectangular UTF-8 CSV, an explicit CC BY 4.0 or CC0 1.0 notice,
and publisher attribution metadata. Large CSVs download at runtime using
the same verified cache. Archive-only and multi-file sources require
separate loaders. Dataset
names and citations come from the publisher. For downstream reuse, cite
the creators and DOI in `dm::datasets::uci_catalog()`.

- [UCI Machine Learning Repository|https://archive.ics.uci.edu/datasets]
- [UCI's API client|https://github.com/uci-ml-repo/ucimlrepo]
- [CC BY 4.0 license|https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/]
